module agentic

# ========================================
# CHANNEL APP TYPE (Organization-scoped)
# ========================================
# Customer-owned messaging-platform apps (a Slack app, a Meta app for
# WhatsApp) that agent channels install through instead of the shared
# platform app (bring your own app, since 2026-07-15). Holds the provider's
# credentials: a Slack app's OAuth client secret and webhook signing
# secret, a Meta app's app secret, access token and verify token.
#
# Access model: RESTRICTED, managed by the organization's current admins
# Channel apps carry the organization's credentials with a messaging
# provider, so they are the organization's credential, not a person's.
# Plain members and viewer-role members of the organization see nothing.
# `owner` is computed, never stored: it is the organization's admins, as
# an OAuth app or a platform client is managed, so an app stays manageable
# whoever created it, and a creator who is demoted below admin or removed
# loses control of it with the role. Rotating or replacing a secret must
# end with the role that allowed it. The creator is recorded in the audit
# trail (kind_meta `owner_type` NONE). Public visibility is intentionally
# unsupported to prevent credential leakage.
#
# An app keeps delivering when its creator leaves: inbound webhooks and
# outbound delivery read the app's secrets as the server, and binding an
# agent channel to an app asks only that both are the organization's.
#
# Permission pattern:
# - Org Admin (and org owner, through admin): full management, secret
#   rotation included. Secrets are redacted on every response.
# - Direct viewer grant: can see the app and who has access to it
# - Org Members and Viewers: no access (administrative resource)
#
# FGA tuple on creation (the kind's creation event: organization scope, no
# owner; private, so no visibility tuple):
# - channel_app:chapp_abc#organization@organization:acme
#
# Checks the handlers make: `can_create_channel_app` on the organization
# to create; `can_view` to get, get by reference, and to keep a row in the
# organization's list; `can_edit` to update; `can_delete` to delete.

type channel_app
  relations
    # ========================================
    # PARENT ORGANIZATION
    # ========================================
    define organization: [organization]

    # ========================================
    # OWNERSHIP
    # ========================================
    # Every current admin of the app's organization, and nobody else.
    define owner: admin from organization

    # ========================================
    # VIEWER ACCESS
    # ========================================
    # Owners (admins included) and direct viewer grants. Organization
    # members and viewers are deliberately absent.
    define viewer: ([identity_account] and affiliated from organization) or owner

    # ========================================
    # PERMISSIONS
    # ========================================
    define can_view: viewer
    define can_edit: owner
    define can_delete: owner

    # ========================================
    # IAM POLICY MANAGEMENT
    # ========================================
    define can_grant_access: owner
    define can_view_access: viewer
